@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Valid signup (expect 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{baseUrl}}

{
  "name": "Paula",
  "email": "paula@example.com",
  "password": "a-long-test-password-123",
  "workSpaceName": "Demo Co"
}

### 2. No Origin header (expect 403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Paula",
  "email": "other@example.com",
  "password": "a-long-test-password-123",
  "workSpaceName": "Demo Co"
}

### 3. Short password (expect 400 with field errors)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{baseUrl}}

{
  "name": "Paula",
  "email": "short@example.com",
  "password": "12345",
  "workSpaceName": "Demo Co"
}


### Login OK (expect 200 and Set-Cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{baseUrl}}

{ "email": "paula@example.com", "password": "a-long-test-password-123" }

### Wrong password (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{baseUrl}}

{ "email": "paula@example.com", "password": "wrong-password-123" }

### Unknown email (expect the same 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{baseUrl}}

{ "email": "nobody@example.com", "password": "wrong-password-123" }

### No Origin (expect 403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "paula@example.com", "password": "a-long-test-password-123" }

### Logout (run Login OK first; expect 204)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{baseUrl}}

### Logout again with no session (expect 204 again)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{baseUrl}}

### Logout without Origin (expect 403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### GET is not allowed (expect 405)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout